id: finance
name: Finance and accounting
industry: Finance & accounting
domain: Financial accounting: ledger, receivables, payables, assets, budgets and reporting
scope: Legal entities and chart of accounts, journal entries, fiscal periods, customers and receivables, suppliers and payables, fixed assets and depreciation, cost and profit centres, budgets, taxes and financial statements.
summary: Describes how an organisation records and reports money: the accounts it keeps, the entries posted to them, what customers owe and suppliers are owed, the assets it holds and how actuals compare with budget. A starter model whose reporting concepts follow IFRS / XBRL.
purpose: Shared vocabulary across ERP finance modules and reporting tools; basis for close, receivables and variance analytics.
read: A Legal entity keeps a Chart of accounts of GL accounts, each of an Account type. A Journal entry in a Fiscal period has balanced Journal lines posting amounts to accounts and optionally a Cost centre. Customer invoices and Receipts form receivables; Supplier bills and Payments form payables. Fixed assets depreciate. Budget lines hold plan amounts; Financial statement lines group accounts for reporting.
in: Ledger and periods; Receivables; Payables; Fixed assets; Cost centres and budgets; Tax; Financial statements
out: Treasury dealing; Payroll calculation; Consolidation eliminations detail; Management costing models
std: xbrl | high | Statement lines and account types follow IFRS / XBRL reporting concepts. | Assets, Liabilities, Equity, Revenue, ProfitLoss, ReportingPeriod
std: fibo | medium | Legal entities and currencies follow FIBO foundations. | LegalEntity, Currency
std: ubl | medium | Invoice structures follow UBL. | Invoice, TaxTotal, PaymentMeans
std: schema | low | Invoices are aligned to schema.org. | schema:Invoice
== Ledger | General ledger | Accounts and entries.
LegalEntity | A company that keeps its own books and reports.
  - entity code : string !
  - name : string !
  - functional currency : string !
  - country : string
ChartOfAccounts | The structured list of accounts used by one or more legal entities.
  - name : string !
  > used by > LegalEntity +
GLAccount | A general ledger account in which amounts of one kind are recorded.
  - account number : string !
  - account name : string !
  - active : boolean
  > in chart > ChartOfAccounts 1
  > of type > AccountType 1
  > rolls up to > GLAccount ?
  > reported in > StatementLine ?
AccountType | The fundamental kind of account.
  * Asset, Liability, Equity, Revenue, Expense
FiscalPeriod | A month or other period of the financial year.
  - period name : string !
  - start date : date !
  - end date : date !
  - fiscal year : gYear !
  > has status > PeriodStatus 1
PeriodStatus | Whether postings are allowed.
  * Open, Closing, Closed
JournalEntry | A dated, balanced set of postings recording one business event.
  - entry number : string !
  - posting date : date !
  - description : string
  - reversed : boolean
  > of entity > LegalEntity 1
  > in period > FiscalPeriod 1
  > from source > JournalSource 1
JournalSource | Where an entry originated.
  * Manual, Receivables, Payables, Assets, Payroll, Inventory, Accrual
JournalLine | One debit or credit to an account within a journal entry.
  - debit amount : decimal
  - credit amount : decimal
  - currency : string
  - narration : string
  > of entry > JournalEntry 1 | | has line
  > posts to > GLAccount 1
  > for cost centre > CostCentre ?
  > for profit centre > ProfitCentre ?
== Receivable | Receivables | What customers owe.
Customer | A party that buys on credit.
  - customer number : string !
  - name : string !
  - credit limit : decimal
  - payment terms days : integer
CustomerInvoice | A bill issued to a customer. | ~schema:Invoice
  - invoice number : string !
  - invoice date : date !
  - due date : date !
  - net amount : decimal !
  - tax amount : decimal
  - outstanding amount : decimal
  > billed to > Customer 1 | | is billed
  > of entity > LegalEntity 1
  > posted as > JournalEntry ?
CustomerReceipt | Money received from a customer.
  - received on : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  > from customer > Customer 1
  > applied to > CustomerInvoice *
== Payable | Payables | What we owe suppliers.
Supplier | A party we buy from on credit.
  - supplier number : string !
  - name : string !
  - payment terms days : integer
SupplierBill | A bill received from a supplier.
  - bill number : string !
  - bill date : date !
  - due date : date !
  - net amount : decimal !
  - tax amount : decimal
  - outstanding amount : decimal
  > from supplier > Supplier 1
  > of entity > LegalEntity 1
  > posted as > JournalEntry ?
SupplierPayment | Money paid to a supplier.
  - paid on : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  > to supplier > Supplier 1
  > settles > SupplierBill *
TaxCode | A tax and rate applied to a transaction.
  - code : string !
  - rate percent : decimal !
  - jurisdiction : string
== Control | Assets, cost centres and budgets | Managing the business.
FixedAsset | A long-lived asset that is capitalised and depreciated.
  - asset number : string !
  - description : string !
  - acquired on : date !
  - cost : decimal !
  - useful life months : integer
  - accumulated depreciation : decimal
  > owned by > LegalEntity 1
  > in class > AssetClass 1
  > assigned to > CostCentre ?
AssetClass | A category of fixed assets with a depreciation rule.
  * Land, Buildings, Plant and machinery, Vehicles, Furniture, IT equipment, Intangibles
CostCentre | A unit of the organisation to which costs are assigned.
  - cost centre code : string !
  - name : string !
  > part of > CostCentre ?
ProfitCentre | A unit of the organisation measured on profit.
  - profit centre code : string !
  - name : string !
BudgetLine | A planned amount for an account and cost centre in a period.
  - amount : decimal !
  - version : string
  > for account > GLAccount 1
  > for cost centre > CostCentre ?
  > in period > FiscalPeriod 1
StatementLine | A line of the balance sheet, income statement or cash-flow statement.
  - line name : string !
  - sequence : integer
  > in statement > StatementType 1
StatementType | The financial statement.
  * Balance sheet, Income statement, Cash flow statement
rule: constraint | Balanced entry | In every journal entry the sum of debit amounts equals the sum of credit amounts. | JournalEntry, JournalLine
rule: constraint | Closed periods | No journal entry can be posted to a period whose status is Closed. | JournalEntry, FiscalPeriod
rule: derivation | Days sales outstanding | DSO is outstanding receivables divided by credit sales, times the days in the period. | CustomerInvoice
rule: derivation | Variance | Variance is actual postings less the budget line for the same account, cost centre and period. | BudgetLine, JournalLine
uc: Receivables ageing | Credit controller | How much do customers owe, by ageing bucket of days overdue? | CustomerInvoice, Customer | billed to, CustomerInvoice.due date, CustomerInvoice.outstanding amount
uc: Actual versus budget | Finance business partner | Where do actual expenses differ from budget by cost centre this period? | JournalLine, JournalEntry, GLAccount, CostCentre, BudgetLine, FiscalPeriod | of entry, posts to, JournalLine.for cost centre, JournalEntry.in period, BudgetLine.for account, BudgetLine.for cost centre, BudgetLine.in period, BudgetLine.amount
uc: Trial balance | Financial controller | What is the balance of every account for a legal entity at period end? | JournalLine, JournalEntry, GLAccount, AccountType, LegalEntity, FiscalPeriod | of entry, posts to, GLAccount.of type, JournalEntry.of entity, JournalEntry.in period, JournalLine.debit amount, JournalLine.credit amount
